es","Seasons this cool ripen Riesling, Müller-Thurgau, Pinot Gris and Gewürztraminer fully without cooking off their freshness."],["Grown here","Riesling sits in its sweet spot, so the wines can show the style it is known for."],["Grown here","Pinot Noir is at its cool limit. In cool years it can stay underripe, with green, sharp flavors."]],"soil":{"rock":"Shale and mudstone are fine-grained rocks that hold heat well and are moderately fertile.","top":"The topsoil holds water well and drains at a steady pace, so vines rarely go thirsty or sit in wet ground. Its pH is close to neutral, so vines take up the nutrients they need easily."},"land":[["Height","The high ground runs about 5°F cooler than the low ground. Higher vineyards ripen later and keep more acidity, so one grape can make lighter or richer wine here depending on height."],["Slope","Gentle slopes. Enough tilt to drain cold air and rain away, which lowers frost risk, yet still easy to farm by machine."]]},"winkler":["Ia","Only very early grapes ripen well, mostly hybrids and a few vinifera."],"wset":true,"sources":[{"name":"Wikidata sitelinks and Wikimedia page views","url":"https://www.wikidata.org"},{"name":"Candiago et al. 2022, A geospatial inventory of regulatory information for wine protected designations of origin in Europe, Scientific Data (product specifications as of 2021)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01513-0"},{"name":"Fick and Hijmans 2017, WorldClim 2.1 monthly averages for 1970 to 2000, 2.5 minute grid (about 4.5 km)","url":"https://www.worldclim.org/data/worldclim21.html"},{"name":"Beck et al. 2023, High-resolution (1 km) Koppen-Geiger maps, Scientific Data (1991 to 2020)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-023-02549-6"},{"name":"Winkler, Cook, Kliewer and Lider 1974, General Viticulture, University of California Press (heat summation regions)","url":null},{"name":"Wikipedia, Winkler index (what each region suits)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Winkler_i